To create a Gmail API application, follow these steps

Step 1: Set Up Google Cloud Console

Step 2: Create a Project
Create a new project by choosing any name that suits your application.

Step 3: Enable Gmail API
Search for "Gmail API" in the console and enable it for your project.

Step 4: Create OAuth Credentials
Set up OAuth credentials to allow your application to interact with Gmail.

Step 5: Configure Application Type
Select the appropriate application type (e.g., Web, Desktop, etc.) during the OAuth setup.

Step 6: Download Credentials
Download the OAuth credentials JSON file after the configuration.

Step 7: Install Required Libraries
Install the necessary Python libraries, such as google-api-python-client and google-auth-httplib2.

Step 8: Authorize API and Generate Token
Use the credentials to authorize the API and generate an access token.

Step 9: Interact with Gmail Account
Start interacting with the Gmail API to send, read, or manage emails in the connected Gmail account.
